<para id="RM0000005A700ZX" category="J" type-id="300N5" name-id="630WU-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Fuel Receiver Gauge Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005A700ZX_14" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000005600000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The combination meter assembly uses the fuel sender gauge assembly to detect the fuel level in the fuel tank. The combination meter assembly outputs battery voltage to the fuel sender gauge assembly via 2 resistors (approximately 1k Ω) connected in parallel inside the meter ECU. The fuel sender gauge assembly has a variable resistor whose resistance changes with the fuel level; it receives voltage from the combination meter assembly and changes the voltage according to the resistance, which varies with the fuel level in the fuel tank. The meter ECU reads the voltage across the variable resistor and the resistor inside the meter ECU, and drives the fuel receiver gauge.</ptxt>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005A700ZX_11" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000005700000">
